messages:
noah: quick sweep request 1: can we review the Model Activity compact rail & the export modal for keyboard traps + SR labels? I noticed focus sometimes disappears when closing modal with ESC. link: https://www.figma.com/file/xyz-compact-rail :mag:

jeni: I checked the compact rail. Tab order looks correct, but when you open the export modal the first focus lands on the close icon (tiny target) instead of the primary CTA. suggest autofocus to the dialog container and set focus to the first focusable CTA.

omar: yep agree. also found 2 SR issues: the export modal doesn't set role="dialog"+aria-modal="true", and the dialog has no accessible name. We should add aria-labelledby pointing to the modal heading.

katie: small visual issue: the CSV/JSON format toggles use light gray borders; in high contrast mode the toggle focus ring blends into the background. propose setting :focus-visible { box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px #004E8C; } and increasing toggle contrast to 3:1 for thumb on track.

jeni: for closing with ESC ensure we remove focus trap before hiding the element so screen readers don't land in a hidden container. Also add inert on the background content while dialog open (or aria-hidden) so VoiceOver doesn't move out-of-dialog.

omar: on that note, the export success toast is announced but not linked to the file download button. Use aria-live="polite" + include a link inside to the artifact with role="link" and an id. toast should also have tabindex="-1" so screen reader can move to it if needed.

a11y-lint-bot: Automated checks: missing role=\"dialog\" and aria-labelledby on export modal (FAIL). ESC close does remove element but focus restored to body rather than triggering focus to the originating trigger (FAIL). Toggle contrast borderline (ratio ~3.0:1) recommend 3.5:1 min for controls. SVG status icons missing <title> (WARN).

katie: for focus restore let's save document.activeElement prior to opening and on close call focus() on that element if still in DOM. If trigger removed, fallback to the next logical control in the rail.

ojeni: also add aria-describedby on the modal to include a short description of what export contains (file size estimate, rows). helps screen reader users decide whether to proceed. keep it short.

omar: small CSS proposal for modal trap & focus: ```js
// save trigger
const opener = document.activeElement;
openDialog();
// set focus to primary button
dialog.querySelector('.primary').focus();
// on close
closeDialog();
if (document.contains(opener)) opener.focus(); else document.querySelector('.model-rail .first-control').focus();
```

jeni: awesome. Noah can you add these to the PR checklist (dialog semantics, focus trap behavior, focus restore, toast link, SVG titles, toggle contrast)? I'll run a quick screen reader pass after PR.

oah: added checklist to PR desc and opened branch. will include code snippets and a11y-lint fixes. thx team! :rocket:
